Ladybird now applies a grid item’s min size to its min-content and
max-content contributions, so a flexible row with a zero minimum
in an indefinite grid grows to its items’ min-height. Blink, WebKit
and Gecko all get a block-axis contribution by measuring the item,
which applies its min-height already: Blink’s GridLayoutAlgorithm::
ContributionSizeForGridItem() lays the item out for measure, WebKit’s
GridTrackSizingAlgorithmStrategy::maxContentContributionForGridItem()
uses logicalHeightForGridItem(), and Gecko’s ContentContribution() in
nsGridContainerFrame.cpp runs a MeasuringReflow() of the item.
